  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Why is My Laundry Room So Dark?",
    "text": "Why is My Laundry Room So Dark?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "If your laundry room feels like a cave, you're not alone! Many homes suffer from inadequate lighting in this often-forgotten space. The main culprit is usually relying on a single, dim overhead fixture. This creates shadows around your washer, dryer, and especially your folding areas, making it hard to see stains or match socks. When you're trying to inspect clothes or navigate around machines, poor visibility can also be a safety concern. Another common mistake is placing lights where they cause glare rather than actually improving visibility. For example, a bare bulb directly overhead might feel bright but casts harsh shadows elsewhere. The goal isn't just 'more light,' it's 'better light.' You want even illumination that eliminates dark zones and makes tasks easier and safer. HH Remodeling LLC understands how proper lighting can transform a functional space like your laundry room, making it much more user-friendly and brighter. Let's shed some light on your laundry day!",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
